check 1: the battery is good enough
check 2: the image is the matched one, its tests pass
step 3: take the phone to fastboot
check 4: the slots' flags are read
step 5: say what to expect
  One command, about 5 minutes: the phone boots the matched UFS-on image once, from memory. It reads the card (its 6 disks and their partition tables), first pins the UFS host's devfreq clock at its lowest, 50 MHz (the userspace governor) and reads it back, then reads sda in steps of 64, 256, 1024 MiB (at most 60 seconds each), read only, a line in its RAM log before each step and the shell polled every second, while the link gear and the clock are noted; a step starts only when it ends before the image's own reboot (180 s after its start, read from the kernel log); the first silent step is a result, the ramp stops there; the disk's partition table is hashed before and after. NOTHING is written to the card. The glass stays dark. The phone returns to Android by itself and visits fastboot once more to read the slot flags; if it is not on Android after 4 minutes, hold the power button about 15 seconds.
check 6: the author's go is recorded on the item
step 7: boot the matched UFS-on image from memory, nothing flashed
check 8: USB device 1d6b:0104 is on the bus
step 9: the shell answers and the image's reboot deadline is read (its init has no hold: it reboots 180 s after its petter starts, research walleye-ufs-180s-is-the-init-self-reboot)
  the image reboots the phone at uptime 181.7 s; now 5.2 s
check 10: the probe lines are in the kernel log
  [    1.347168] ufshcd-qcom 1da4000.ufshc: UFS_HW_VERSION 3.1.0
  [    1.347215] ufshcd-qcom 1da4000.ufshc: UFS_HOST_LEFT HCS 0x0000010f HCE 0x00000001
  [    1.347269] qcom-qmp-ufs-phy 1da7000.phy: UFS host 3.1.0: MSM8998 PHY table 3.1.0
  [    1.359945] qcom-qmp-ufs-phy 1da7000.phy: UFS_PHY_LINECFG_DISABLE 0x00000000
