step 16: the UFS host's devfreq clock is pinned low (userspace governor, set_freq 50 MHz read back, gear HS_GEAR1, cur_freq 50 or 100 MHz as core_clk's rounding: research walleye-ufs-pin-100mhz-read) and its evidence kept, before any load
  1da4000.ufshc: governor simple_ondemand, clock 50000000 -> governor userspace, clock 100000000 (gear HS_GEAR1)
  gear-pinned.txt: gear HS_GEAR1 lanes 2 rate HS_RATE_B mode FAST_MODE link_state HIBERN8 dev_pm ACTIVE; clock 100000000
step 17: a ramped, bounded, read-only read of the disk (each step only when its limit ends before the image's reboot deadline less 10 s, its start uptime kept), a RAM log line before each step, the shell polled every second, the gear sampled
